WEBVTT

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:18.600
Do you hear?  Hooves beating

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:30.750
A carriage goes through the gentle hills

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:37.980
Someone comes to pick me up

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:45.950
And takes me

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.900
To the avenue with white flowers

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:58.050
To the home of wind

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:02.400
He takes me

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.900
I'm sure

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:36.630
Monday and Tuesday great preparations
went on at Green Gables.

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:40.720
Having the minister and his wife to tea
was a serious and important undertaking,

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:46.240
and Marilla was determined not to be
eclipsed by any of the Avonlea housekeepers.

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:52.120
Anne was wild with excitement and
delight for helping Marilla,

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:59.460
and also because she was going to
make a cake for Mrs. Allan.

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:06.040
Marilla and Anne were very carefull so
Matthew didn't know anything about it.

00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:11.920
They were afraid he would find an excuse
to be away that day if he knew about it.

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:17.920
On Tuesday evening Anne talked it all over
with Diana by the Dryad's Bubble.

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:20.520
Everything is ready, Diana,

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:24.550
except my cake which I'm
to make in the morning.

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:30.270
Marilla and I have had a busy two days of it.

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:34.410
It's such a responsibility having
a minister's family to tea.

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:37.860
We're going to have jellied chicken

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:39.970
and cold tongue.

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:42.760
We're to have two kinds of jelly,
red and yellow,

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:46.970
and whipped cream and lemon pie,
and cherry pie,

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:50.100
and three kinds of cookies,
and fruit cake.

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:56.100
And Marilla's famous yellow plum
preserves, and pound cake,

00:02:56.100 --> 00:03:00.230
and biscuits as aforesaid,
and my layer cake.

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:02.550
My! Twelve different things?

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:07.790
But I just grow cold when
I think of my layer cake.

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:11.840
Oh, what will I do if it's not good?

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:14.140
Diana, I dreamed last night

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:19.920
that I was chased all around by a fearful
goblin with a big layer cake for a head.

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:24.890
A cake goblin?

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:28.320
But, Anne, It'll be good, all right.

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:30.360
Do you really think so, Diana?

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:35.620
Yes, because the one you made that
we had for lunch in Idlewild two weeks ago

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:37.280
was perfectly elegant.

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:41.460
Diana, you're a best friend indeed!

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:48.210
But cakes have a habit of turning out bad just
when you especially want them to be good.

00:03:49.070 --> 00:03:53.940
I shall just have to trust to Providence
and be careful to put in the flour.

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:02.970
Oh, look, Diana, what a lovely rainbow!

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:04.520
It really is.

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:27.040
Do you suppose the dryad will come out
after we go away and take it for a scarf?

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:31.170
But, Anne, you know there is
no such thing as a dryad.

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:38.820
But, Diana, it's so easy to imagine there is.

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:43.750
Every night before I go to bed,
I look out of my window...

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:48.110
...and wonder if the dryad is
really sitting here,

00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:52.080
combing her locks with the
spring for a mirror.

00:05:09.210 --> 00:05:16.130
Sometimes I look for her footprints
in the dew in the morning.

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:18.880
And did you find any, Anne?

00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:24.440
Oh, Diana, don't give up
your faith in the dryad!

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:31.750
All right.

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:34.780
If you believe it, I'll believe it too.

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:48.190
Wednesday morning came.

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:05.480
What's wrong? Did I catch a cold?

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:10.780
Good morning, Marilla.

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:14.960
Why are you up so early, Anne?

00:06:15.820 --> 00:06:18.530
But Mrs. Allan is coming today,

00:06:18.530 --> 00:06:20.640
so I can't sleep.

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:27.110
She will be here only in the afternoon.
We still have much time.

00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:30.380
What's wrong?

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:32.830
I wonder if I caught a cold.

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:37.600
It must be because of your dabbling in the
spring on the preceding evening, with Diana.

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:38.950
What should I do?

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:41.790
I have to make my important cake.

00:06:42.430 --> 00:06:45.800
Well, calm down.
Everything is almost done,

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:47.660
so you don't need to worry.

00:06:47.780 --> 00:06:49.170
Go sleep some more.

00:06:50.380 --> 00:06:51.870
I can't do that.

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:56.880
Anne finally stopped sneezing at breakfast,

00:06:56.880 --> 00:07:00.310
but she was with a terrible cold.

00:07:02.620 --> 00:07:09.450
Matthew, we invited the new minister
and his wife for tea this afternoon.

00:07:10.710 --> 00:07:14.390
Do you understand?
You have to be present.

00:07:14.390 --> 00:07:16.070
W-well I...

00:07:16.070 --> 00:07:19.490
I have to take care of the mare.

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:22.270
Matthew, please! You have to be here!

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:26.600
Don't be like that, Matthew.
You are the head of this house.

00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:28.520
We... well now, yes.

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:32.350
But... I'm not good with these things.

00:07:32.350 --> 00:07:36.150
I... I'd better... not be present.

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:37.380
Matthew!

00:07:39.030 --> 00:07:41.080
We made so much good food.

00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:44.090
And they're both very nice people!

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:47.350
Well? You'll be here, won't you?

00:07:47.410 --> 00:07:51.020
Well now... how could I...

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:54.300
Just tell them... well...

00:07:54.510 --> 00:07:57.170
that I have flu and I'm resting.

00:07:59.990 --> 00:08:04.680
If Matthew is not present, today's
meeting won't be so interesting, Marilla!

00:08:07.490 --> 00:08:09.480
I'm going to bring Matthew here.

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:10.220
Forget it.

00:08:10.670 --> 00:08:13.350
Matthew won't change his
mind if he's so set on it.

00:08:13.810 --> 00:08:17.530
And if you don't hurry up and tidy this place
up, you won't have time to make your cake.

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:47.230
This is really yeast?

00:09:25.650 --> 00:09:26.560
It's ready?

00:09:42.460 --> 00:09:45.800
I'm sure I haven't forgotten
anything this time, Marilla.

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:50.560
But do you think it will rise?

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:53.630
Just suppose perhaps
the baking powder isn't good?

00:09:54.510 --> 00:09:57.220
I used it out of the new can.

00:09:57.510 --> 00:10:01.060
Mrs. Lynde says you can never be sure of
getting good baking powder nowadays

00:10:01.060 --> 00:10:04.060
when everything is so adulterated.

00:10:04.600 --> 00:10:07.760
She says the Government
ought to take the matter up.

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:11.930
We'll let the matter of the Government rest.

00:10:12.100 --> 00:10:13.340
How is your cold?

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:16.570
My cold is almost gone.

00:10:16.890 --> 00:10:21.520
But Marilla, what if that cake doesn't rise?
What should we do?

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:23.450
Don't worry.

00:10:23.860 --> 00:10:26.470
We'll have plenty without it.

00:10:32.540 --> 00:10:35.550
The cake did rise, however,

00:10:35.880 --> 00:10:40.430
and came out of the oven as light and
feathery as golden foam.

00:10:41.190 --> 00:10:46.980
Anne, flushed with delight, clapped
it together with layers of ruby jelly.

00:10:56.770 --> 00:11:04.210
And, in imagination, Anne saw Mrs. Allan eating
it and possibly asking for another piece!

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:09.490
This is truly delicious!

00:11:09.630 --> 00:11:11.630
Anne, could I have one more please?

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:13.640
Yes. Of course, Mrs. Allan!

00:11:15.100 --> 00:11:17.440
I wish to have one more too.

00:11:21.340 --> 00:11:22.780
Marilla!

00:11:28.010 --> 00:11:29.300
The cake is done.

00:11:29.590 --> 00:11:31.200
Put it over there.

00:11:39.820 --> 00:11:43.220
You'll be using the best tea set, of course.

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:46.930
Don't touch it.
I just polished it bright.

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:54.440
Marilla.
Can I fix the table with ferns and wild roses?

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:56.720
Fix the table with ferns and wild roses?

00:11:57.040 --> 00:11:58.260
I think that's all nonsense.

00:11:58.620 --> 00:12:03.580
In my opinion it's the eatables
that matter and not flummery decorations.

00:12:04.210 --> 00:12:06.680
Mrs. Barry had HER table decorated,

00:12:06.980 --> 00:12:10.390
and the minister paid her an
elegant compliment.

00:12:10.910 --> 00:12:14.320
He said it was a feast for
the eye as well as the palate.

00:12:14.730 --> 00:12:16.810
Well, do as you like.

00:12:17.380 --> 00:12:20.810
Only mind you leave enough
room for the dishes and the food.

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:23.540
Yes. I know.

00:12:24.360 --> 00:12:26.690
Tidy up all the utensils used on the cake.

00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:43.900
I forgot. I can't smell anything today.

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:04.570
Anne hopes the tea to be a success

00:13:05.280 --> 00:13:09.860
and wanted Matthew
to take part no matter what.

00:13:42.270 --> 00:13:43.950
Matthew, are you ready?

00:13:44.520 --> 00:13:46.270
My. You look great, Matthew.

00:13:46.690 --> 00:13:48.810
Just like the day you came to fetch me.

00:13:48.950 --> 00:13:50.270
Well now...

00:13:50.690 --> 00:13:52.060
This...

00:13:53.240 --> 00:13:54.760
How do I put this...

00:13:55.300 --> 00:13:56.970
It's all right.
Let me help you.

00:13:58.080 --> 00:13:59.980
Marilla will be surprised.

00:14:00.300 --> 00:14:02.820
She thinks you will lie on bed all day.

00:14:03.600 --> 00:14:08.000
Well now.
I was... But you...

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:09.300
Anne! Anne!

00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:11.270
Where are you?
The guests are here!

00:14:12.140 --> 00:14:13.460
Come on. Let's go.

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:19.100
I won't go out just yet.

00:14:19.380 --> 00:14:20.300
Matthew!

00:14:20.300 --> 00:14:21.000
Anne!

00:14:22.180 --> 00:14:23.360
You must come!

00:14:31.650 --> 00:14:37.670
Marilla and Anne stood outside
the house to welcome the guests.

00:14:38.220 --> 00:14:44.190
Anne forgot about Matthew
now that Mrs. Allan was here.

00:14:45.380 --> 00:14:48.440
My brother isn't feeling very well today.

00:14:49.380 --> 00:14:51.050
I'm sorry to hear that.

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:52.560
Please come in.

00:14:56.970 --> 00:14:58.670
Matthew Cuthbert!

00:14:58.670 --> 00:15:00.100
Matthew!

00:15:03.100 --> 00:15:04.960
Welcome, Mr. Allan.

00:15:05.360 --> 00:15:07.130
This is my brother Matthew.

00:15:08.010 --> 00:15:10.310
Pleased to meet you.
I'm minister Allan.

00:15:11.450 --> 00:15:13.380
How is your illness?

00:15:14.790 --> 00:15:19.930
Well... I... I feel better now.

00:15:20.800 --> 00:15:23.070
Well, please come in.

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:40.560
What a beautiful table!

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:47.740
It has a very fragrant smell.

00:15:48.060 --> 00:15:52.540
It's very beautiful.
Thank you for doing this for us.

00:15:53.370 --> 00:15:55.160
It's Anne's doings.

00:15:55.970 --> 00:15:58.680
You must be an artist, Anne Shirley.

00:16:07.360 --> 00:16:09.500
Thank you very much, Mrs. Allan.

00:16:10.130 --> 00:16:11.590
I'm the one who is thankful.

00:16:15.540 --> 00:16:17.600
Anne was very happy.

00:16:18.110 --> 00:16:19.540
And Matthew too.

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:23.700
Unlike Marilla thought, he talked
to the minister with interest.

00:16:24.220 --> 00:16:28.220
He never said a word to Mrs. Allan,

00:16:28.220 --> 00:16:31.700
but that perhaps was not to be expected.

00:16:33.780 --> 00:16:38.790
All went merry as a marriage bell

00:16:38.790 --> 00:16:42.350
until Anne's layer cake was passed.

00:16:42.880 --> 00:16:44.790
Please have a piece of cake.

00:16:46.160 --> 00:16:50.360
I'm already full.
I don't think I can eat more.

00:16:52.560 --> 00:16:56.570
Oh, you must take a piece of this, Mrs. Allan.

00:16:56.570 --> 00:16:59.690
Anne made it on purpose for you.

00:16:59.690 --> 00:17:02.280
Oh, In that case I must sample it.

00:17:08.980 --> 00:17:10.970
It looks delicious.

00:17:28.040 --> 00:17:29.100
Anne Shirley!

00:17:31.120 --> 00:17:33.950
What on earth did you put into that cake?

00:17:34.560 --> 00:17:37.150
Nothing but what the recipe said, Marilla.

00:17:37.310 --> 00:17:38.540
Isn't it all right?

00:17:38.540 --> 00:17:42.750
It's simply horrible.
Mrs. Allan, don't try to eat it.

00:17:43.480 --> 00:17:46.210
Anne, what flavoring did you use?

00:17:46.270 --> 00:17:47.500
Vanilla.

00:17:56.120 --> 00:18:00.530
Oh, Marilla, it must have been the baking
powder. I had my suspicions of that bak...

00:18:00.530 --> 00:18:02.560
Baking powder fiddlesticks!

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:05.570
Go and bring me the bottle
of vanilla you used.

00:18:17.940 --> 00:18:19.420
It's really vanilla.

00:18:19.870 --> 00:18:21.170
Let me see.

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:31.710
Mercy on us!

00:18:32.900 --> 00:18:38.050
Anne, you've flavored that cake
with ANODYNE LINIMENT.

00:18:38.730 --> 00:18:40.670
It was on the medicines shelf, wasn't it?

00:18:40.920 --> 00:18:42.120
Yes.

00:18:43.310 --> 00:18:45.930
I broke the liniment bottle last week and

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:49.050
poured what was left into an
old empty vanilla bottle.

00:18:49.290 --> 00:18:54.160
I suppose it's partly my fault.
I should have warned you.

00:18:55.170 --> 00:18:58.260
But why couldn't you have smelled it?

00:19:00.070 --> 00:19:01.980
I couldn't.

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:05.540
I had such a cold!

00:19:06.030 --> 00:19:07.690
Hey! Anne!

00:19:41.690 --> 00:19:45.980
Oh, Marilla, I'm disgraced forever.

00:19:46.310 --> 00:19:49.030
I shall never be able to live this down.

00:19:49.140 --> 00:19:55.700
It will get out--things always
do get out in Avonlea.

00:19:56.760 --> 00:20:00.320
Diana will ask me how my cake turned out

00:20:00.320 --> 00:20:03.530
and I shall have to tell her the truth.

00:20:03.900 --> 00:20:11.550
I shall always be pointed at as the girl
who flavored a cake with anodyne liniment.

00:20:16.380 --> 00:20:17.470
Oh, Marilla,

00:20:17.470 --> 00:20:20.620
if you have a spark of Christian pity

00:20:20.620 --> 00:20:24.990
don't tell me that I must go
down and wash the dishes after this.

00:20:26.790 --> 00:20:30.160
I'll wash them when the
minister and his wife are gone.

00:20:31.440 --> 00:20:35.890
But I cannot ever look
Mrs. Allan in the face again.

00:20:36.840 --> 00:20:42.080
Perhaps she'll think I tried to poison her.

00:20:42.080 --> 00:20:48.420
Mrs. Lynde says she knows an orphan
girl who tried to poison her benefactor.

00:20:50.900 --> 00:20:53.770
But the liniment isn't poisonous.

00:20:54.490 --> 00:20:58.100
Won't you tell Mrs. Allan so, Marilla?

00:20:59.160 --> 00:21:02.240
Suppose you jump up and tell her so yourself?

00:21:04.580 --> 00:21:05.890
Mrs. Allan!

00:21:08.800 --> 00:21:10.180
Anne Shirley.

00:21:11.080 --> 00:21:13.500
My dear little girl,
you mustn't cry like this.

00:21:13.900 --> 00:21:18.270
Why, it's all just a funny mistake
that anybody might make.

00:21:24.100 --> 00:21:28.610
Oh, no, it takes me to make such a mistake.

00:21:29.010 --> 00:21:33.820
And I wanted to have that
cake so nice for you, Mrs. Allan.

00:21:33.820 --> 00:21:35.720
Yes, I know, dear.

00:21:35.990 --> 00:21:41.420
And I assure you I appreciate
your kindness and thoughtfulness

00:21:41.420 --> 00:21:43.160
just as much as if it had turned out all right.

00:21:46.650 --> 00:21:49.490
Now, you mustn't cry any more,

00:21:49.840 --> 00:21:54.530
but come down with me
and show me your flower garden.

00:21:54.600 --> 00:21:58.470
Miss Cuthbert tells me
you have a little plot all your own.

00:22:02.140 --> 00:22:03.710
I want to see it,

00:22:03.980 --> 00:22:06.030
for I'm very much interested in flowers.

00:22:10.850 --> 00:22:12.510
Mrs. Allan!

00:22:25.530 --> 00:22:30.100
Anne permitted herself to
be led down and comforted,

00:22:30.100 --> 00:22:36.410
reflecting that it was really providential
that Mrs. Allan was a kindred spirit.

00:22:37.100 --> 00:22:41.480
Nothing more was said about
the liniment cake.

00:22:52.520 --> 00:22:58.010
And when the guests went away, Anne said...

00:22:58.820 --> 00:23:04.580
Marilla, isn't it nice to think that tomorrow
is a new day with no mistakes in it yet?

00:23:04.580 --> 00:23:08.520
I'll warrant you'll make plenty in it.

00:23:09.020 --> 00:23:12.500
I never saw your beat for making mistakes.

00:23:12.590 --> 00:23:14.270
Yes, and well I know it.

00:23:14.300 --> 00:23:18.530
But have you ever noticed one
encouraging thing about me, Marilla?

00:23:18.530 --> 00:23:19.720
I don't see what.

00:23:19.720 --> 00:23:23.200
I never make the same mistake twice.

00:23:24.000 --> 00:23:25.350
My, my...

00:23:26.490 --> 00:23:30.740
I don't know as that's much benefit when
you're always making new ones.

00:23:30.810 --> 00:23:32.840
Oh, don't you see, Marilla?

00:23:32.840 --> 00:23:36.240
There must be a limit to the mistakes
one person can make.

00:23:36.740 --> 00:23:38.880
That's a very comforting thought.

00:23:39.160 --> 00:23:42.300
Well, you'd better go and
give that cake to the pigs.

00:23:42.300 --> 00:23:45.340
It isn't fit for any human to eat.

00:23:45.340 --> 00:23:48.680
All right. I'll give it to the pigs
and apologise to them.

00:23:54.270 --> 00:24:00.900
Anne found that she had enjoyed the evening
more than could have been expected.

00:24:01.520 --> 00:24:05.410
And why was that?
Even Anne herself didn't know why.

00:24:17.560 --> 00:24:23.100
Anne went to the post office and
got a letter adressed to her.

00:24:23.290 --> 00:24:26.350
Next episode of
Anne of Green Gables:

00:24:26.350 --> 00:24:28.040
Anne is Invited Out to Tea

00:24:28.040 --> 00:24:29.310
Please watch!
